cyMAE — Cytometry Masked Autoencoder
====================================

Source:   https://github.com/JaesikKim/cyMAE
Commit:   7f28acea14934fb7202bc9440b25f7e8e5ef7b2e
License:  Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE)
Citation: Kim et al., bioRxiv 2024.02.13.580114v2

Files vendored from upstream
----------------------------
- modeling_pretrain.py   (PretrainVisionTransformer encoder + decoder + factories)
- modeling_finetune.py   (Block, Mlp, Attention, _cfg, get_sinusoid_encoding_table; finetune
                          VisionTransformer also defined but not used by us)
- masking_generator.py   (RandomMaskingGenerator)

Modifications
-------------
- modeling_pretrain.py: import line changed from
      `from modeling_finetune import Block, _cfg, get_sinusoid_encoding_table`
  to
      `from .modeling_finetune import Block, _cfg, get_sinusoid_encoding_table`
  so the package can be loaded as a Python sub-package.

- modeling_pretrain.py: non-learnable sinusoid `pos_embed` registered as a
  non-persistent buffer in both `PretrainVisionTransformerEncoder` and the
  `PretrainVisionTransformer` wrapper (was a plain tensor attribute upstream).
  The corresponding `forward_features` / `forward` calls drop the per-step
  `.type_as(x).to(x.device).clone().detach()` and now use a single
  `.to(dtype=x.dtype)`. This removes a host↔device alloc per forward and is
  checkpoint-compatible (`persistent=False` keeps it out of state_dict).

Files NOT vendored
------------------
- engine_for_pretraining.py / engine_for_finetuning.py / optim_factory.py / utils.py
  We write our own training loops in src/baselines/cyMAE/{pretrain,train_heads}.py
  using plain AdamW; we do not use the upstream engines / distributed utilities /
  tensorboard logging.
- run_mae_pretraining.py / run_class_finetuning.py
  CLI replaced by our own scripts that integrate with BenchmarkLoader.
- dataset_folder.py / datasets.py
  Replaced by data.py (parquet adapter).
